WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
- [Kelly] Hello! So baby
number three is on the way?

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.410
- Yeah. My wife is gonna love that intro.

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.030
- Yeah. She should be a little scared.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.920
I always think like, because I have two,

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.713
and I'm outnumbered
because I'm single now,

00:00:09.713 --> 00:00:11.760
but it's a different thing
when you're outnumbered.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.260
You're like, no one's there to like ...

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.420
You know, you only have so many arms.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.520
- [Topher] Yes. Everyone
says like on the first baby,

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:19.426
they're like, "Oh, congratulations!"

00:00:19.426 --> 00:00:20.259
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:20.259 --> 00:00:21.390
- Then the second baby, they're
like, "Congratulations."

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.286
On the third baby there's, like,
a question mark at the end.

00:00:23.286 --> 00:00:25.620
They're like, "Congratulations?"

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.000
- So where should I send the flower?

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.060
- [Topher] Yeah, it's
... But we're excited.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.110
My wife is ...

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.730
I'll just take this moment
on national television

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:34.431
to say how beautiful and amazing she is.

00:00:34.431 --> 00:00:35.645
- [Kelly] Aw!

00:00:35.645 --> 00:00:36.560
(crowd cheering)

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:37.770
I love that.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.060
That's exciting, though. It is cool.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.380
Like your family's just
getting even bigger.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.220
That's cool.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.921
- Yeah. Check in with me in about ...

00:00:42.921 --> 00:00:43.770
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- One year.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.120
- [Kelly] And you're
gonna be like so tired.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:45.953
Yeah.

00:00:45.953 --> 00:00:47.190
It is cool though because the siblings.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.023
Like, I have two kids,

00:00:48.023 --> 00:00:49.680
and they literally want
me to have another baby.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.600
They get excited. They
want a baby in the house.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.070
- That's like how I wanted my parents to

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:54.217
get a dog so bad, and I was like,

00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:56.340
"I will participate.

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.930
Like, I will walk the dog.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.139
- Yeah. And then you didn't.

00:00:59.139 --> 00:00:59.972
- [Topher] And then I did nothing.

00:00:59.972 --> 00:01:00.805
- No.

00:01:00.805 --> 00:01:01.638
- The whole ... I think I
walked that dog one time.

00:01:01.638 --> 00:01:03.810
- [Kelly] My daughter suckered
me into that, as well.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.370
I think she prepped me with,
"You should have a baby."

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:06.720
And I was like, "Oh!"

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:07.650
- [Topher] We'll get a dog.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.000
- And then she was like,
"Or how about just a puppy?"

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.440
And I was like, "You're good."

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:11.460
I was like, "Okay."

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.360
So we got another one,

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:14.850
and she said she'd help, and she lied.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:18.060
As a parent, though, are
you pro, like, screen time?

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.140
Are you, like, pro that?

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.360
Or like, are you trying to,
you know, steer clear of it?

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.850
- We're trying to do as little
screen time as possible.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.490
We were real, like, no screen time people.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:27.493
- [Kelly] That's how we all start.

00:01:27.493 --> 00:01:28.326
- [Topher] Yeah, exactly. That's how.

00:01:28.326 --> 00:01:30.450
- Yeah. And then you're
like, I need to pee.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:31.650
- [Topher] Yeah, exactly.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:32.610
- [Kelly] Watch this.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.770
But wait, did your parents
let you have screen time?

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:35.603
Did you watch TV?

00:01:35.603 --> 00:01:38.610
- No, I am a product of ...

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.760
It was not zero screen time.
My mom loved old movies.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.368
- Yeah. Classics.

00:01:43.368 --> 00:01:44.340
- [Topher] My mom, another wonderful woman

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.600
I'd love to shout out.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.970
And she only let me watch classic movies,

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.737
which sounds like a good
move, and was, ultimately,

00:01:50.737 --> 00:01:53.550
great that I wasn't watching a lot of TV,

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.770
but I only watched old movies.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.500
I had, like, a lot of Cary
Grant, a lot of Danny Kay.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.333
- Love!

00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:00.900
- Yeah. But I would go into school,

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.280
and, like, I remember one time,

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.730
like, in seventh grade, I
used the term "man alive"

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:07.500
which is like a, you know,
when something bad happens,

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.476
you go "man alive" in, like, the forties.

00:02:09.476 --> 00:02:10.710
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:12.420
- And I started to realize, like,

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:15.450
TV is, like, how you normalize people.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.950
They get to know, like, what
the vernacular is like now.

00:02:17.950 --> 00:02:18.783
- [Kelly] Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:18.783 --> 00:02:21.540
- And so, I went to boarding
school when I was a teenager,

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.888
and then I watched TV for,
like, three years nonstop.

00:02:24.888 --> 00:02:25.920
- To catch up?

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:26.753
- [Topher] To catch up and say,

00:02:26.753 --> 00:02:27.857
"Oh this is how people
of modern day talk."

00:02:27.857 --> 00:02:29.100
- You're right, though!

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:29.933
Yeah.

00:02:29.933 --> 00:02:30.766
But you're right, though.

00:02:30.766 --> 00:02:31.599
That is, like, how friendships ...

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:32.550
Like, you talk about the same thing.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:33.383
You have this,

00:02:33.383 --> 00:02:34.620
"Oh, did you see that
episode when this happened?"

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:35.453
You're true. Yeah, that's true.

00:02:35.453 --> 00:02:36.286
- [Topher] All the kids
are saying ... Yeah.

00:02:36.286 --> 00:02:37.350
Did you see In Living Color?

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:39.164
Did you see Saturday Night Live?

00:02:39.164 --> 00:02:40.140
- [Kelly] ♪ In living color ♪

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:41.707
- Yeah. And I had no idea
what they were talking about.

00:02:41.707 --> 00:02:45.120
And then, and then I just,
like, binged everything

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.604
that had ever been made once I was away.

00:02:46.604 --> 00:02:47.437
- [Kelly] Okay. Well done.

00:02:47.437 --> 00:02:50.197
- But anyway, my mom was
wonderful. I'm glad she did it.

00:02:50.197 --> 00:02:51.900
- I think she had great
taste is what that is.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:52.733
Yeah.

00:02:52.733 --> 00:02:53.730
- Actually I didn't tell you.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:54.720
This is, uh ...

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:58.950
My mom told me that Saltines were cookies.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.540
Which was smart.

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:01.373
- Were you poor?

00:03:01.373 --> 00:03:02.264
Because I feel like my mom did that.

00:03:02.264 --> 00:03:03.186
- [Topher] Nope!

00:03:03.186 --> 00:03:04.019
- [Kelly] Oh. Because I was like,

00:03:04.019 --> 00:03:04.852
"I feel like my mom did that."

00:03:04.852 --> 00:03:05.685
And we used to do this.

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:06.518
It was like poor man's dessert,

00:03:06.518 --> 00:03:07.560
and you'd have, like, a little butter and

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.330
like, a marshmallow, and
you'd put it in the microwave,

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.621
and it was like dessert.

00:03:10.621 --> 00:03:11.730
(Topher and crowd laughing)

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:12.563
Yeah.

00:03:12.563 --> 00:03:13.680
- No, my mom just thought, like ...

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:14.820
I mean she had all the right ideas

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:17.010
She was like, "Let's
keep these kids healthy."

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.530
And so she ... I'd go, "Can
I have a cookie please?"

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:21.150
And she give me a Saltine. I'd say, "Yum!"

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:21.996
And then ...

00:03:21.996 --> 00:03:22.829
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:22.829 --> 00:03:25.140
And then when I was,
like, six or something,

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.780
I went on my first
sleepover to a kid's house,

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.350
and this kid was like,
"That's not a cookie.

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:33.960
This is a cookie." And
it was, like an Oreo,

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:35.340
And I was like, "What is that?"

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:37.410
And she had to come pick me
up because I couldn't sleep.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.786
Like had so much sugar in my ...

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:40.973
I ate like the whole thing of Oreos.

00:03:40.973 --> 00:03:42.630
- [Kelly] Because it's so bad. Yeah.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:44.510
But did your mom make you
take classes or anything?

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:47.190
Like, you know, like,
sports or music or anything?

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.780
- Well, this was something that a lot

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:52.290
of kids did at this school
I grew up at in Connecticut.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.650
There's, like, a cotillion,
like, ballroom dancing class.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:59.250
- You definitely weren't
poor. Because nope.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.413
No poor people even
know what cotillion is.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:03.503
I still don't.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:05.580
- You're not wrong, Kelly.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:09.960
But it wasn't my thing,
just to let you know.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:11.850
Like, I wasn't into it,

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.370
But it was the only thing
that boys and girls could do

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:15.630
in that town together.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.220
It was ... I don't know,
some guys showed up ...

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.510
- [Kelly] What, were you
in the movie Footloose?

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.010
Like, wait, what?

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.160
- No, no. This was a pro-dance thing.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:26.040
But sadly, it was just,
like, ballroom dancing.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.473
- [Kelly] Oh, that's cool!

00:04:27.473 --> 00:04:30.600
- It was not cool, but
it was ... it was ...

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.640
Again, I'd seen in these
movies I watched growing up,

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:33.630
So I thought, "Oh, that'll be cool."

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:35.730
And then I was so bad at it, I kind of ...

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:39.630
There was a kid who -
on national television,

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.970
I will call Frank, but
that's not his name,

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.530
and you know who you are, Frank -

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:46.430
who, like, made fun of me a lot

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:49.140
because I didn't get the
ballroom dancing steps right

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:49.973
or whatever.

00:04:49.973 --> 00:04:51.210
I still think I was cooler than him,

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:54.330
but he was technically much
more popular than I was.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:59.330
But then when I started acting,
I guess I did one movie,

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:02.370
and then my second film
was Mona Lisa Smile,

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.203
if anyone remembers that.

00:05:03.203 --> 00:05:04.500
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh! I love that one.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.911
- And I have to dance with
Julia Roberts in this movie.

00:05:06.911 --> 00:05:07.744
- [Kelly] Damn!

00:05:07.744 --> 00:05:08.887
- And so they said like,

00:05:08.887 --> 00:05:10.680
"Will you, like, before filming starts?"

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:11.793
And I was already just
terrified to meet her.

00:05:11.793 --> 00:05:15.720
They were like, "Will you come
do a ballroom dancing class

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:16.553
with Julia Roberts?"

00:05:16.553 --> 00:05:18.327
And I was like, "This is my shot."

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.060
I was like, "Everything
I learned in that ..."

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:22.980
Oh! here we are dancing.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:23.813
It's me and my ...

00:05:23.813 --> 00:05:25.080
- [Kelly] Look at your little baby face!

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:26.130
- [Topher] Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:26.963
I was so scared.

00:05:26.963 --> 00:05:29.520
I stepped on her toes,
like, a couple times,

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.260
and she was very cool about it.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.510
And then when we did it on the day,

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:36.300
the whole cast was also
dancing on the dance floor.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:39.330
And again, I won't use his
name, but I told her this story,

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:41.490
and Julia Roberts came up to
me at the end after the scene,

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:44.280
and she high fived me and she
goes, "That was for Frank."

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:45.780
And I was like ...

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.960
- [Kelly] Ah! We can't stand
Frank, whoever you are.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:49.890
- Frank, you know who you are!

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.720
- [Kelly] Yeah. Bullying isn't cool.

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:54.270
That was a look at season
three of your show,

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:55.230
Home Economics.

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.570
You can see it Wednesdays on ABC.

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:59.820
So you asked to show that clip, right?

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:00.900
That was the clip you
wanted to show, right?

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:04.680
- Yes. Because that
episode, our fourth episode,

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.600
takes place in 2009.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:08.292
That might explain why we looked ...

00:06:08.292 --> 00:06:09.330
- [Kelly] Awesome.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:10.163
- Awesome.

00:06:10.163 --> 00:06:11.770
- That ... the swing. That was amazing.

00:06:11.770 --> 00:06:13.610
- [Topher] Yeah, and they put
so much product in my hair

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:15.217
the hair lady was like,

00:06:15.217 --> 00:06:17.117
"Don't stand next to any open flames."

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:23.003
But we're trying to clear
some Kelly Clarkson, 2009.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.160
Don't worry, I won't make
you agree to anything.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:28.183
- I know. I'm like, "Well, I'll agree."

00:06:28.183 --> 00:06:29.016
What is it?

00:06:29.016 --> 00:06:29.849
- That's the album, right?

00:06:29.849 --> 00:06:31.085
That's the ... what is that?

00:06:31.085 --> 00:06:31.918
- [Kelly] Yeah, 2009
was ... what was that?

00:06:31.918 --> 00:06:32.751
- What was that? My Life
Would Suck Without You.

00:06:32.751 --> 00:06:33.780
- [Kelly] Yeah, that All I Wanted.

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:36.353
Ooo, I should know this. Yep! Ooo.

00:06:36.353 --> 00:06:37.710
I don't listen to myself.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.981
- [Topher] That's right.
Yeah. That would be weird.

00:06:39.981 --> 00:06:40.814
- Yeah. That would be weird

00:06:40.814 --> 00:06:41.910
if I'm just, like, jamming to myself.

00:06:41.910 --> 00:06:43.320
But I think I listened to it too much.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:44.970
But that ... I'll get it cleared.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:45.803
- [Topher] Great.
- Yeah.

00:06:45.803 --> 00:06:46.636
- All right. Great. You
heard it. You're it here.

00:06:46.636 --> 00:06:47.470
- [Kelly] You heard it here.

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:49.380
Clearing songs is hard!

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:51.120
Do you know how many
songs I do on this show?

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.312
Clearing songs can be difficult.

00:06:52.312 --> 00:06:53.370
- Oh, yeah. Half the work.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:54.210
- Yeah.

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:55.043
- After I came last time,

00:06:55.043 --> 00:06:56.670
I had such a great time on your show,

00:06:56.670 --> 00:07:00.270
and Wilmer Valderrama had
just been on before me,

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:01.140
and we were talking about it,

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:05.460
and we can't believe that we
weren't hanging out with you.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:09.720
Like, I feel like 2009
was ... or mid-2000s,

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.160
like I can't believe
we never crossed path,

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:11.993
and what I said to him, I was like,

00:07:11.993 --> 00:07:14.400
"I think we would've,
like, hung out with her."

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.480
- We totally would've hung out.

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:16.710
Here's the thing about to know about me,

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:20.274
I am an extrovert, but
also secretly an introvert.

00:07:20.274 --> 00:07:22.650
- That just means you're an introvert.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:24.218
- [Kelly] No, I know,
but I am an extrovert.

00:07:24.218 --> 00:07:27.210
It's like, once I get to know someone,

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:28.740
then I'm like this all the time.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.600
I think on camera I'm even more outgoing

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.610
than I am in life.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:34.702
- I think that's a lot
of actors that I meet.

00:07:34.702 --> 00:07:36.600
- Well, I'm not an actor, but
musicians are like that, too.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.760
- What was the ... when was the ...

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:39.720
You're singing in the rain.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.250
I was talking to your
producer about this, like,

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:44.250
it's, like, raining indoors,
and you're singing at like,

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:45.247
MTV Movie Awards.

00:07:45.247 --> 00:07:46.167
- [Kelly] Hazel Eyes ... no.

00:07:46.167 --> 00:07:47.040
- But no, it's like a ...

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:48.090
- Oh, Since U Been Gone!

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:49.140
- [Topher] Yeah, but when was that?

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:50.670
- [Kelly] That was the VMAs.

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:51.810
- [Topher] That's, like,
the greatest performance

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:52.680
of that time.

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:55.110
That's up there, for me,
with, like, Prince Super Bowl.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.219
Sorry, I don't mean to ...

00:07:56.219 --> 00:07:58.126
(crowd cheering)

00:07:58.126 --> 00:07:59.626
